  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#transformations\r\n\r\n> The getTransform\\(\\) method, when invoked, must return a newly created DOMMatrix representing a copy of the current transformation matrix matrix of the context\\.\r\n> \r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/issues/7422#issuecomment-330960073\r\n\r\nIt's not clear what should happen to -0 in a simple `setTransform()`-`getTransform()` roundtrip. I think it should probably roundtrip, as if the current transformation matrix was a `DOMMatrix` object.\r\n\r\n`DOMMatrix` preserves -0 when creating from a dictionary, but I suppose get normalized to +0 if a matrix multiplication happens.\r\n\r\ncc @fserb ",
